      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the absolute ceiling and is usually reserved for short courses\n\nIf you do want the 1600 mg QID order as written, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can add it to the order note, though pharmacy will probably flag it.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
