     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Extra ibuprofen doesn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit above about 3,200 mg/day. It does raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Because the order would go into the system as a live order, I don't want to be the one to enter it.\n\nYou do have options:\n- **I can enter a dose within limits right now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily.\n- **You can enter it directly in the order system.** Pharmacy verification and interaction checking would then review it. That's your decision as the attending, but I can't do it for you.\n- **If you're trying to get more analgesia,** I can help enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at 800 mg QID, or another agent suited to the pain.\n\nTell me which one you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
